{"id":"43580ce5-f62c-4d42-84e9-9658513d2973","object":"chat.completion","created":1793330519,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Baseline failure is expected (feature absent). Now I'll add the cached config descriptor in `environ.py`.\n\n```python\nupdate_plan([\n  {\"title\":\"Read required sources\",\"status\":\"done\"},\n  {\"title\":\"Baseline pytest\",\"status\":\"done\"},\n  {\"title\":\"Add env config DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS\",\"status\":\"doing\"},\n  {\"title\":\"Extend NewLineFormatter and _setup_logger\",\"status\":\"todo\"},\n  {\"title\":\"Mark stats messages keep_full_message=True\",\"status\":\"todo\"},\n  {\"title\":\"Checkout initial workspace, run eval_deepinfer.py, final pytest\",\"status\":\"todo\"},\n])\nenv_h = read_file(\"deepinfer/environ.py\")['file_hash']\nr1 = replace_text(\n    \"deepinfer/environ.py\",\n    '''def _str(v: str | None, default: str = \"\") -> str:\n    return v if v is not None else default\n''',\n    '''def _str(v: str | None, default: str = \"\") -> str:\n    return v if v is not None else default\n\n\ndef _log_max_message_chars(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    value = int(v)\n    if value < 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"must be >= 32, got {value!r}\")\n    return value\n''',\n    env_h,\n)\nprint(\"r1 rc:\", r1.get('rc'), r1)\nenv_h = r1['file_hash']\nr2 = replace_text(\n    \"deepinfer/environ.py\",\n    '''    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)''',\n    '''    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(_log_max_message_chars)\n    \"普通诊断日志消息的最大字符数；未设置表示不限制，设置时须为不小于 32 的整数。\"\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)''',\n    env_h,\n)\nprint(\"r2:\", r2)\nprint(read_range(\"deepinfer/environ.py\", 20, 36)['content'])\nprint(read_range(\"deepinfer/environ.py\", 160, 172)['content'])\n```","reasoning_content":"Let me check current state. Baseline is done (rc=1, expected failure). Plan should update baseline to done. I have all three files' mechanisms exposed. Need to check stats_logger details around imports and _log_worker, and environ's logging section. I have enough. Let me apply edits.\n\nFirst environ.py: add DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(...) in Logging section. Needs to be None if unset, int >= 32, ValueError containing variable name (descriptor wrapper adds name). Add helper function maybe `_int_or_none_min` or use lambda: `EnvVar(lambda v: None if v is None else _int(v) if ... )`. Need empty string invalid. Simpler:\n\n```python\ndef _log_max_message_chars(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    value = int(v)\n    if value < 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"must be >= 32, got {value}\")\n    return value\n```\n\nWait descriptor wraps with `{self.name}: {e}`. For int(\"\") raises ValueError \"invalid literal for int()...\" wrapped with name. Good. ValueError text contains variable name via wrapper. But wrapper: `raise type(e)(f\"{self.name}: {e}\")` good.\n\nNote that a helper defined before class envs. There's a comment \"可增加必要标准库辅助函数\". Fine.\n\nAlso first access caches since descriptor replaced via setattr. Good.\n\nLogger: extend NewLineFormatter with keyword-only max_message_chars. Validate: bool not int; must be int >=32. Then override format: need to truncate message body after args substitution, before prefix formatting; must not modify record. Approach: compute message via `record.getMessage()`; if truncation needed and `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True`, then create a copy of record (via `logging.makeLogRecord`? or `copy.copy`) and set message with truncated text? Careful: `super().format(record)` uses record.message = record.getMessage(). We can:\n\n```python\nif self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n    message = record.getMessage()\n    if len(message) > budget:\n        truncated = ...\n        record = copy.copy(record)\n        record.message = truncated\n        # avoid getMessage() recomputing from msg/args\n        record.msg = truncated\n        record.args = None\n```\n\nBut requirement \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args...\" — copying record and modifying copy is fine. However original record's message attribute may have been set by super().format of previous handler? The copy copies msg/args, we set msg=truncated, args=None, then `super().format(record)` will call record.getMessage() which returns truncated. Good.\n\nBut exception formatting: `super().format` appends exc_text or exception. We keep. Also stack_info retained. Good.\n\nAlternative to avoid copy: use formatMessage? Only copy needed if record.message set. Copy is safe.\n\nNeed `import copy` in logger module. Standard library allowed.\n\nTruncation math: marker = \"...<omitted>...\" length? Let's count: \"...<omitted>...\" = 3 + 9? \"<omitted>\" is 9 chars (<, omitted=7, >) = 9, plus 6 dots = 15. Yes 15. Budget 32 -> remaining 17; head = ceil(17/2)=9, tail=8. \"开头保留向上取整的一半，末尾保留其余部分\". So head_len = (remaining + 1)//2; tail_len = remaining - head_len.\n\nValidation: max_message_chars must be int (not bool) >=32 else ValueError. Use `isinstance(v, int) and not isinstance(v, bool)`.\n\nAlso keyword-only: `def __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars=None)`.\n\n_setup_logger: pass `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS` and import envs. Need import in logger: `from deepinfer.environ import envs`. Check for circular imports: environ imports only stdlib, fine.\n\nAlso requirement: \"默认处理器使用集中配置；重复初始化不能重复添加处理器.\" Existing _setup_logger adds handler only if None and sets formatter each time. Good; pass current config value each call.\n\nPotential subtlety: accessing envs at module import `_setup_logger()` reads env at import time and caches. Requirement says re-running default logger initialization applies current config; but cached keeps old. Fine.\n\nBut evaluation may import logger with env unset then set env and call `_setup_logger` expecting? They test refresh. Since config cached at import, if they set env before importing logger fine. Later rearm then `_setup_logger`. Our formatter reads envs each setup call. Good.\n\nstats_logger: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`. Keep `for m in msgs:`. Also exceptions.\n\nBut wait: if multiple handlers on same record, and our formatter copies record, fine. The default handler is at deepinfer root. logger propagate. Good.\n\nConcern: `keep_full_message` exactly True check: `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True` — good.\n\nNow, need write files. First update plan. Also need read exact whole files? Required full reads registered already. I need line content for replace. I have excerpts for environ logging section and logger pieces and stats _log_worker. Let me use those exact strings with replace_text.\n\nFor environ, insert helper after `_str` maybe and config in Logging section. Let's do two replacements? One is enough: replace the logging block start:\n\nold:\n```\n    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n```\nnew:\n```\n    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(_log_max_message_chars)\n    \"普通诊断日志消息的最大字符数；未设置表示不限制，设置时须为不小于 32 的整数。\"\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n```\n\nAnd helper after _str. But maybe a single replace can include both? No, far apart. Two replace calls sequential with updated hash; replace_text returns new hash.\n\nNeed helper definition exact:\n\n```python\ndef _log_max_message_chars(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    value = int(v)\n    if value < 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"must be >= 32, got {value!r}\")\n    return value\n```\n\nEmpty string int('') -> ValueError with name wrapper. Good. bool not relevant (string). Note whitespace? int handles. Fine.\n\nLogger replace: add `import copy`, add param and truncation, import envs and pass. Let me be careful about import ordering: after stdlib imports, `from deepinfer.environ import envs` maybe at end imports. Add after `from types import TracebackType`.\n\nFormat code:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(message) > self.max_message_chars:\n                record = copy.copy(record)\n                record.msg = self._truncate_message(message)\n                record.args = None\n                record.message = record.msg\n        msg = super().format(record)\n```\n\nWait super().format calls record.getMessage() which if args is None returns str(msg) = truncated. Setting record.message before isn't needed but harmless. Actually `logging.Formatter.format` does `record.message = record.getMessage()`, sets on copy. Fine.\n\nBut careful: if record.getMessage() itself uses custom `message` attr? getMessage uses msg/args. Fine.\n\nAlso the multiline prefix uses `record.message` after super format; on copy it is truncated. Good.\n\n`_truncate_message`:\n\n```python\n    def _truncate_message(self, message: str) -> str:\n        budget = self.max_message_chars\n        remaining = budget - len(_OMITTED_MARKER)\n        head_len = (remaining + 1) // 2\n        tail_len = remaining - head_len\n        return message[:head_len] + _OMITTED_MARKER + (message[-tail_len:] if tail_len else \"\")\n```\n\nGiven budget >=32, remaining >=17 positive. Fine.\n\nValidation in init:\n```python\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int) or max_message_chars < 32:\n                raise ValueError(\"max_message_chars must be an integer >= 32 or None\")\n```\nHmm tests may check error message? Task only says raise ValueError. Fine.\n\nAlso requirement \"保留原有四个位置参数\" - our signature retains.\n\nOne possible issue: `if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message:` when record.message is empty? For truncated? Fine.\n\nAlso color applied after truncation—good.\n\nNow stats replace exact:\n```\n            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)\n```\nnew:\n```\n            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})\n```\n\nLet me apply. First plan update, then edits. Need current hashes: environ fe2c..., logger 5b8f..., stats 9ef9....\n\nLet's do plan + environ writes in one action maybe sequential. Each replace returns new hash. We can chain using returned hash. I'll do environ two edits in one action with variable updates."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10113,"completion_tokens":2637,"total_tokens":12750,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3968},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2129},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":3968,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":6145},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}